    "details_title": "Tool and holder",
    "details": [
      "5 \u00d7 5 OOBB grid. Each half is 4 mm thick. The assembled holder is 8 mm thick.",
      "Print the supplied two-half layout once. Face the pockets inward and align the mounting holes. With the opening at the top, lower the tool into the assembled holder.",
      "Turn each key so its short arm points forward, then align the long arm over its sized bore.",
      "Each key rests at its own bore floor and all six short arms remain accessible.",
      "The holder specifies the hex size. Arm lengths follow the Wiha 350 short series as a representative example. The holder source leaves the key manufacturer unspecified. The elbow is simplified.",
      "Digital check: the seated tool occupies the pocket with no measurable solid overlap.",
      "AI-generated CAD images and instructions. Physical fit has yet to be tested.",
      "See the holder README for the dimensions and OOMP references of every tool."
    ],
